# Module `identity`

## Owns

The person record with roles (T3-D-009), credentials, sessions, consents, preferences, pets, consultations. PostgreSQL schema `identity`.

## Public API (`index.ts`) <!-- verified: exports -->

| Export | Use |
|---|---|
| `createIdentity({ repo, bus, clock })` | Builds the module service |
| `.registerPerson({ email, givenName, familyName, brand? })` | Creates a person. Publishes `identity.person-registered` |
| `.getPerson(id)` | Reads a person or `null` |
| `InMemoryPersonRepository` | Store for tests and the fixture |
| `EmailAlreadyRegisteredError` | Thrown when the e-mail exists |
| `Identity`, `IdentityDeps`, `RegisterPersonInput` | Types of the service |
| `Person`, `PersonRepository`, `PersonRegistered` | Types of the record, the store and the event |

## Tables (`schema.ts`)

| Table | Personal columns |
|---|---|
| `identity.person` | `email`, `given_name`, `family_name` |

## Events <!-- verified: events -->

| Event | Direction | Payload |
|---|---|---|
| `identity.person-registered` | Emits | `personId`, `brand` |

## Invariants

- One person record per e-mail address. The e-mail is stored in lower case (T3-AC-003).
- At most one ERP customer number per person (T3-AC-003).
- ERP master data comes through the `integration` module, never from the ERP port.

## Acceptance criteria

T3-AC-003, T3-AC-004.
import { pgSchema, text, timestamp, uuid } from "drizzle-orm/pg-core";
import { notPersonal, withDataMeta } from "../kernel";

export const identitySchema = pgSchema("identity");

export const persons = withDataMeta(
  identitySchema.table("person", {
    id: uuid("id").primaryKey(),
    email: text("email").notNull().unique(),
    givenName: text("given_name").notNull(),
    familyName: text("family_name").notNull(),
    erpCustomerNumber: text("erp_customer_number").unique(),
    brand: text("brand").notNull(),
    createdAt: timestamp("created_at", { withTimezone: true }).notNull(),
  }),
  {
    id: notPersonal,
    email: {
      personal: true,
      category: "contact",
      purpose: "Sign-in and account e-mails",
      owner: "identity",
      retention: "account lifetime + 3 years",
    },
    givenName: {
      personal: true,
      category: "identity",
      purpose: "Address the person and fulfil orders",
      owner: "identity",
      retention: "account lifetime + 3 years",
    },
    familyName: {
      personal: true,
      category: "identity",
      purpose: "Address the person and fulfil orders",
      owner: "identity",
      retention: "account lifetime + 3 years",
    },
    erpCustomerNumber: notPersonal,
    brand: notPersonal,
    createdAt: notPersonal,
  },
);
import { type Clock, type EventBus, newId, systemClock } from "../kernel";
import type { Person, PersonRegistered, PersonRepository } from "./person";

export interface RegisterPersonInput {
  email: string;
  givenName: string;
  familyName: string;
  brand?: string;
}

export class EmailAlreadyRegisteredError extends Error {
  constructor() {
    super("A person with this e-mail exists");
    this.name = "EmailAlreadyRegisteredError";
  }
}

export interface IdentityDeps {
  repo: PersonRepository;
  bus: EventBus;
  clock?: Clock;
}

export function createIdentity({ repo, bus, clock = systemClock }: IdentityDeps) {
  return {
    /** One person record per e-mail address (T3-D-009). */
    async registerPerson(input: RegisterPersonInput): Promise<Person> {
      const email = input.email.trim().toLowerCase();
      if (await repo.findByEmail(email)) throw new EmailAlreadyRegisteredError();
      const now = clock.now();
      const person: Person = {
        id: newId(now),
        email,
        givenName: input.givenName,
        familyName: input.familyName,
        erpCustomerNumber: null,
        brand: input.brand ?? "provital",
        createdAt: now.toISOString(),
      };
      await repo.insert(person);
      const event: PersonRegistered = {
        type: "identity.person-registered",
        id: newId(now),
        occurredAt: now.toISOString(),
        payload: { personId: person.id, brand: person.brand },
      };
      await bus.publish(event);
      return person;
    },

    async getPerson(id: string): Promise<Person | null> {
      return repo.findById(id);
    },
  };
}

export type Identity = ReturnType<typeof createIdentity>;
export type { Person, PersonRegistered, PersonRepository } from "./person";
export { InMemoryPersonRepository } from "./person";
export type { Identity, IdentityDeps, RegisterPersonInput } from "./service";
export { createIdentity, EmailAlreadyRegisteredError } from "./service";
export interface DomainEvent<TType extends string = string, TPayload = unknown> {
  readonly type: TType;
  readonly id: string;
  readonly occurredAt: string;
  readonly payload: TPayload;
}

export type EventHandler<E extends DomainEvent> = (event: E) => void | Promise<void>;

/**
 * The queue between modules. Production uses pg-boss through the outbox;
 * tests and the fixture use the in-memory bus.
 */
export interface EventBus {
  publish(event: DomainEvent): Promise<void>;
  subscribe<E extends DomainEvent>(type: E["type"], handler: EventHandler<E>): void;
}

export class InMemoryEventBus implements EventBus {
  private readonly handlers = new Map<string, EventHandler<DomainEvent>[]>();
  readonly published: DomainEvent[] = [];

  async publish(event: DomainEvent): Promise<void> {
    this.published.push(event);
    for (const handler of this.handlers.get(event.type) ?? []) {
      await handler(event);
    }
  }

  subscribe<E extends DomainEvent>(type: E["type"], handler: EventHandler<E>): void {
    const list = this.handlers.get(type) ?? [];
    list.push(handler as EventHandler<DomainEvent>);
    this.handlers.set(type, list);
  }
}
# Data conventions

Source: [architecture.md section 5](../architecture.md#5-data), ADR-0011, TD-09.

## Tables

- Each module owns one PostgreSQL schema. Define tables in `packages/core/src/<module>/schema.ts` with Drizzle.
- A module never reads another module's tables. Use the other module's public API.
- **Every table is wrapped in `withDataMeta(table, meta)`** from `kernel`. `meta` has one entry per column.
- A column that is not personal data: `notPersonal`.
- A personal data column:

  ```ts
  phone: {
    personal: true,
    category: "contact",           // contact | identity | preference | financial | health | other
    purpose: "Contact about an order",            // why the platform keeps it
    owner: "identity",             // the module that owns it
    retention: "account lifetime + 3 years",          // how long the platform keeps it
  },
  ```

- Personal data is any value that identifies a person or is about a person: names, e-mail, phone, address, date of birth, bank details, IP address, consent choices.
- `pnpm pii` fails when a column has no metadata, when a personal column has an empty purpose, owner or retention, or when a column name shows personal data but the metadata says `personal: false`.
- Default retention for account data: `account lifetime + 3 years`. Consent records: `account lifetime + 3 years` (proof of consent).

## Values

- **Money** is an integer in minor units with a currency: `kernel.money(amountMinor)`. Never a float.
- **Time** is stored in UTC as an ISO string. A business date uses the `Europe/Berlin` calendar: `kernel.businessDate(instant)`.
- **IDs** are UUIDv7: `kernel.newId(now)`. ERP keys (customer number `K123456`, advisor number `B12345`) are separate columns.
- **Brand**: entities that a second brand would split have a `brand` column (T3-D-013).
